# Normalize line endings.
#
# The repo already stores every text file with LF in the index. Without this
# file, a Windows checkout under `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF in
# the WORKING TREE, which git then hides (it compares post-normalization) but
# Prettier does not — its default `endOfLine: "lf"` fails `npm run format:check`
# on files nobody edited. Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the working tree matching the
# index, so the format gate reflects real formatting rather than the OS that
# happened to clone the repo.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git decide what is text; only the checkout EOL is
# forced. Binary assets are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so git never line-ending-normalizes them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
